**1. Trailer gate on the commit-snapshot capture** (hooks_git_cmd.go): before running `captureCommitSnapshotsForInFlightTasks`, read HEAD's commit message (one CommitObject) and SKIP the capture when it carries no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer — condensation only happens for trailer-bearing commits (PostCommit bails at manual_commit_hooks.go:947), so a human's no-trailer commit currently pays a full analyzer scan + full sanitize→redact transcript storage for nothing (turn-end already backstops freshness). Comment states exactly that cost rationale. Use the existing trailer-parsing helper (`trailers.ParseCheckpoint` — find how PostCommit itself reads it and reuse).

**2. Staleness bound on marker trust.** The ACTIVE shape is bounded by `isRecentInteraction`; idle+marker is currently trusted forever — an orphaned marker (subagent died without SubagentStop, parent stays alive-idle) would keep linking every future no-TTY commit indefinitely. Decision: introduce a file-local helper in strategy (also resolving the reviewer's minor #3 duplication):
```go
// idleWithLiveMarker reports whether state is an IDLE session with a
// recently-started background task — the second shape trusted to link and
// condense commits without overlap evidence. Bounded by the marker's age:
// markers are cleared only by final captures (SubagentStop/SessionEnd), so a
// subagent that dies without either leaves its marker behind; an unbounded
// trust would link every later no-TTY commit into the session forever. 24h
// matches activeSessionInteractionThreshold's generosity; the sweep-finalize
// follow-up (see PR body) is the eventual hygiene for orphaned markers.
